# Swift 6 Strict Concurrency

## Common Errors & Fixes

### "Compiler unable to type-check this expression"
SwiftUI `body` gets too complex. Fix by extracting into computed properties:
```swift
// BAD - body with 15+ modifiers or nested views
var body: some View {
    ZStack { ... }
        .onChange(of: x) { ... }
        .onChange(of: y) { ... }
        // 10 more modifiers...
}

// GOOD - extract views and use ViewModifiers
var body: some View {
    rootContent
        .modifier(MyEventHandlers(...))
}

private var rootContent: some View { ... }
```

### "Sending 'self' risks causing data races"
Can't capture `self` in async closures from non-isolated classes. Avoid `DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter` with `[weak self]`.

```swift
// BAD
DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter(deadline: .now() + 0.1) { [weak self] in
    self?.doThing()
}

// GOOD - do it synchronously if possible
doThing()

// OR - if delay needed, mark class @MainActor
@MainActor class MyService { ... }
```

### "Static property is not concurrency-safe"
Mutable static vars need explicit annotation:
```swift
// BAD
private static var cache: [String: Data]? = nil

// GOOD
private nonisolated(unsafe) static var cache: [String: Data]? = nil
```

### ViewModifier body too complex
Same fix - split into multiple smaller modifiers:
```swift
// BAD - one modifier with 10+ .onChange
struct AllHandlers: ViewModifier {
    func body(content: Content) -> some View {
        content
            .onChange(...) // x10
    }
}

// GOOD - group by concern
struct KeyboardHandlers: ViewModifier { ... }
struct AudioHandlers: ViewModifier { ... }
```

## Audio Engine

### Device Changes
AVAudioEngine stops working when audio device changes. Listen and restart:
```swift
NotificationCenter.default.addObserver(
    forName: .AVAudioEngineConfigurationChange,
    object: engine,
    queue: .main
) { _ in
    tearDown()
    setupAudio()
}
```

### Render Block Safety
NO Swift classes or locks in AVAudioSourceNode render block:
```swift
// Capture primitives before the block
let sr = Float(sampleRate)
let engineRef = synth // class pointer is fine, just don't alloc inside

sourceNode = AVAudioSourceNode { _, _, frameCount, bufferList in
    // Only use captured values and raw pointers here
}
```
